1. PURPOSE

This repository publishes a bounded public browser laboratory, teaching surface, technical specimens, validation fixtures, receipt machinery, Pixel Witness machinery, schemas, source-bound explanatory materials, and related public technical documentation.

This Notice establishes the boundary between public inspection and commercial or production rights.

This repository is source-available for the limited purposes expressly stated below.

It is not released under an open-source license.

2. PROTECTED MATERIALS

"Protected Materials" means the original copyrightable expression contained in this repository, including:

- source code;
- HTML;
- CSS;
- JavaScript;
- original written material;
- original selection, organization, and arrangement;
- validation fixtures;
- receipt formats;
- original schemas;
- Pixel Witness implementation;
- evidence structures;
- teaching layers;
- technical documentation;
- original diagrams and graphics;
- generated witness encodings to the extent protectable;
- test structures;
- original software implementations;
- original indexing and addressability structures;
- and other original material owned or controlled by Kevin Flint / Latent Studios.

Protected Materials do not include third-party works except to the extent that Kevin Flint / Latent Studios owns a separate original protectable contribution.

3. LIMITED PUBLIC INSPECTION LICENSE

Subject to this Notice, permission is granted to:

a. view and execute the publicly hosted browser laboratory;

b. view the public repository;

c. fork the public repository through GitHub to the extent required or permitted by GitHub's platform functionality and applicable GitHub terms;

d. download or clone the repository for noncommercial inspection, archival, security review, interoperability analysis, procurement review, regulatory review, prior-art review, scholarly review, teaching, and evaluation;

e. quote and cite reasonable portions of the Protected Materials for criticism, commentary, scholarship, review, or attribution;

f. execute the unmodified public fixtures locally for noncommercial evaluation and reproducibility review; and

g. retain archival copies for evidentiary, scholarly, regulatory, procurement, or prior-art purposes.

These permissions are limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, and do not include commercial or production rights.

